    "description": "Worked in collaboration with facility to conduct national research to investigate how college students utilize internet resources to enhance learning and success.\n• Performed Quantitative and Qualitative data analysis on survey data using Microsoft Excel, and Nvivo software to highlight trends in the data. Analysis found that 45% of respondents utilized the internet for help with mathematics compared to other college classes.\n• Crafted weekly presentations of data, utilizing pivot tables to neatly organize qualitative data in bar charts. Suggested insights based upon trends observed in the data to enhance presentations effectiveness.\n• Coordinated survey outreach via compiling research contacts to increase percentage of survey respondents by 20%. Improved information gathering process leading to a reduction in time during contact compilation.\n• Weekly deliverables led to Co-Author on an abstract paper submitted and published to MAA’s 2022 Mathfest Conference.",
